cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CCRP DataSet, please cite this dataset and the accompanying paper."
title: "Chinese Character Riddle Probes Dataset (CCRP DataSet)"
type: dataset
# The dataset content version is 0.1 and does not change between patch
# releases. v0.1.1 is a documentation-only repository patch (see CHANGELOG.md).
version: "0.1"
date-released: "2026-11-09"
license:
  - CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - name: "Spring Buds Data Source Inc."
    alias: "春芽数源"
    country: CN
abstract: >-
  A 100-character Chinese character riddle dataset for behavioral structural
  probing of large language models. Contains 1,019 CC-Riddle-derived reference
  riddles with character structure cards, 600 model-authored riddles with
  quality-control verdicts, a 597-item generation-solving closed loop with
  cross-model blind test and same-item self-test, and a 24-item ICL control
  task (192 API calls). Released under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 for the data, MIT for
  the scripts, CC BY 4.0 for the documentation. This is a diagnostic probe,
  not a ranking benchmark.
keywords:
  - Chinese character riddles
  - structural probe
  - large language models
  - behavioral probe
  - control task
  - generation-solving closed loop
  - in-context learning
  - dataset
repository-code: "https://github.com/SunSeeding/ccrp"
url: "https://github.com/SunSeeding/ccrp"
# Zenodo DOI is intentionally omitted until the deposition is published.
# After Zenodo assigns 10.5281/zenodo.<id>, uncomment and fill:
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.<id>"
# See docs/ZENODO.md for the archiving and backfill procedure.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "汉字字谜能否成为大语言模型的结构探针？"
  authors:
    - name: "Spring Buds Data Source Inc."
      alias: "春芽数源"
  year: 2026
  note: >-
    English translation: "Can Chinese Character Riddles Serve as Structural
    Probes for Large Language Models?". Both editions are included as
    paper/riddle-paper{,-en}.md, with typeset .html and .pdf editions.
